Let us be precise about what was taken and what was not.

  Taken     : the idea that "a menu bar animal runs faster the busier the
              system is", and the shape of the formula that turns load into
              a frame interval (interval = 500 / max(1, load/5)).

  Not taken : any code or artwork. RunCat365 is a Windows WinForms app whose
              measurement layer sits on Windows-only PerformanceCounter, so
              there was nothing reusable on macOS. Every animal sprite was
              drawn from scratch (tools/gen_sprites.py).

